<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="0.56" dur="5.44">I would uh I have prepared just a few</text><text start="2.56" dur="5.12">remarks to welcome our honored guest and</text><text start="6" dur="4.719">I&amp;#39;d like to greet of course the</text><text start="7.68" dur="6.8">honorable Donald J. Trump, the president</text><text start="10.719" dur="6.4">of the United States, your majesty, your</text><text start="14.48" dur="5.52">excellencies. Good evening to you all at</text><text start="17.119" dur="6.801">this extremely important night.</text><text start="20" dur="7.84">Well, uh to we just had the closing</text><text start="23.92" dur="6">ceremonies of Azan 49 and it has been a</text><text start="27.84" dur="4.719">full and very rewarding week here in</text><text start="29.92" dur="4.639">Manila. We convened with our friends and</text><text start="32.559" dur="4.561">partners from across the world and spent</text><text start="34.559" dur="5.84">the days listening to one another and</text><text start="37.12" dur="5.52">finding new ways to work together. And</text><text start="40.399" dur="4.401">uh as I have said this afternoon, our</text><text start="42.64" dur="6.079">partners have become a very important</text><text start="44.8" dur="6.48">part of the wider Azan family and it is</text><text start="48.719" dur="7.761">a pleasure to close the year in good</text><text start="51.28" dur="8">company and in a special summit that we</text><text start="56.48" dur="5.84">have put together in honor of the the</text><text start="59.28" dur="5.839">arrival of President Trump. So President</text><text start="62.32" dur="5.28">Trump, once again on behalf of Azan, it</text><text start="65.119" dur="5.68">is our great pleasure to welcome you to</text><text start="67.6" dur="5.44">Manila. Your presence confirms what we</text><text start="70.799" dur="4.881">already know that Azan and the United</text><text start="73.04" dur="5.04">States are partners in shaping the</text><text start="75.68" dur="4.479">region&amp;#39;s future.</text><text start="78.08" dur="5.52">We in the Philippines know this</text><text start="80.159" dur="5.681">friendship well. This year we mark 80</text><text start="83.6" dur="5.199">years of diplomatic relations between</text><text start="85.84" dur="5.84">our two countries. Our relations have</text><text start="88.799" dur="5.521">have rested on shared history, shared</text><text start="91.68" dur="4.72">values, and the ties that continue to</text><text start="94.32" dur="5.28">bind our peoples, including the millions</text><text start="96.4" dur="8.079">of Filipinos and Filipino Americans who</text><text start="99.6" dur="7.6">live in it every single day. For Azan,</text><text start="104.479" dur="6.241">the partnership reaches even further,</text><text start="107.2" dur="6.48">spanning trade, investment, technology,</text><text start="110.72" dur="4.96">security, and in the case certainly of</text><text start="113.68" dur="3.84">the Philippines. When I&amp;#39;m asked, &amp;quot;What</text><text start="115.68" dur="4.64">is the most important part of your</text><text start="117.52" dur="5.84">relationship with the United States?&amp;quot; I</text><text start="120.32" dur="5.439">cannot answer the question because there</text><text start="123.36" dur="5.2">is no part of our lives in the</text><text start="125.759" dur="5.921">Philippines that is not involved with</text><text start="128.56" dur="5.679">the United States in some way in some</text><text start="131.68" dur="5.12">shape or form or another. And that is</text><text start="134.239" dur="5.201">how deep that partnership has gone and</text><text start="136.8" dur="7.12">that is how deep the partnership will</text><text start="139.44" dur="6.879">continue to go. And uh next year, Azan</text><text start="143.92" dur="5.36">and the United States mark 50 years of</text><text start="146.319" dur="5.841">dialogue relations and 5 years of</text><text start="149.28" dur="5.2">comprehensive strategic partnership.</text><text start="152.16" dur="4.96">And before I finish, I would just like</text><text start="154.48" dur="5.119">to make a very simple announcement in</text><text start="157.12" dur="7.199">anticipation of your arrival, Mr.</text><text start="159.599" dur="7.761">president and we knowing your your</text><text start="164.319" dur="7.601">desire for results</text><text start="167.36" dur="7.2">uh and not uh just talk we uh our staffs</text><text start="171.92" dur="5.039">have been working together asan and uh</text><text start="174.56" dur="6.319">your staffs have been working together</text><text start="176.959" dur="6.64">and uh we have come to uh uh to been</text><text start="180.879" dur="5.921">able to finalize and have adop adopted</text><text start="183.599" dur="7.201">the principles to tackle online scams</text><text start="186.8" dur="6.88">and also we have We have adopted the</text><text start="190.8" dur="4.88">statement on 10 public private</text><text start="193.68" dur="4.639">partnerships principles on tackling</text><text start="195.68" dur="5.76">online scams and the comprehensive work</text><text start="198.319" dur="6.801">plan. And so that is an immediate result</text><text start="201.44" dur="6.4">of this special summit between Azan and</text><text start="205.12" dur="4.479">the United States. And we look forward</text><text start="207.84" dur="4.479">to celebrating all the milestones</text><text start="209.599" dur="5.121">between Azan and the United States and</text><text start="212.319" dur="5.2">the Philippines and the United States.</text><text start="214.72" dur="5.439">and we look forward to continuing to</text><text start="217.519" dur="5.841">have you as our friend and as our</text><text start="220.159" dur="7.321">partner. Thank you and welcome again,</text><text start="223.36" dur="4.12">President Trump to Manila.</text><text start="244.239" dur="4.881">Well, thank you very much. It&amp;#39;s an honor</text><text start="246.319" dur="4.721">to be here and so many friends that I&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="249.12" dur="4.319">known for now a long time. I&amp;#39;ve been</text><text start="251.04" dur="5.12">doing this for all of a sudden it seems</text><text start="253.439" dur="5.76">like a long time, but I&amp;#39;ve gotten to</text><text start="256.16" dur="5.919">know most of you and you&amp;#39;ve done a</text><text start="259.199" dur="6.081">fantastic job running your countries,</text><text start="262.079" dur="5.12">your levels of popularity, and it isn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="265.28" dur="3.44">easy, but you&amp;#39;ve done a great job. So,</text><text start="267.199" dur="5.681">it&amp;#39;s an honor to be with you. And I want</text><text start="268.72" dur="8.64">to thank President Marcus for his</text><text start="272.88" dur="7.599">beautiful welcome to Manila and ASEAN</text><text start="277.36" dur="4.64">summit. It&amp;#39;s uh become very important</text><text start="280.479" dur="3.041">all over the world right now. They&amp;#39;re</text><text start="282" dur="5.759">talking about your country. You know</text><text start="283.52" dur="6.16">that. And they&amp;#39;re talking about uh ASEAN</text><text start="287.759" dur="5.361">and for his excellent leadership as</text><text start="289.68" dur="6.32">chair of ASEAN. This year has been a</text><text start="293.12" dur="4.639">record year. It&amp;#39;s a true pleasure to be</text><text start="296" dur="5.6">back in the Philippines. I&amp;#39;ve been here</text><text start="297.759" dur="5.601">numerous times and uh I just don&amp;#39;t want</text><text start="301.6" dur="5.36">to date myself but I knew your parents</text><text start="303.36" dur="5.92">very well and uh they were great. I</text><text start="306.96" dur="4.48">believe in genetics and they did a good</text><text start="309.28" dur="4.4">job. You have very good genetics. I can</text><text start="311.44" dur="5.52">tell you that. But one of America&amp;#39;s</text><text start="313.68" dur="6.48">oldest and most important allies of of</text><text start="316.96" dur="6.959">uh our country and frankly of the world.</text><text start="320.16" dur="6.96">The United States is a Pacific nation in</text><text start="323.919" dur="6">a true sense and we have been engaged in</text><text start="327.12" dur="6.799">trade and commerce and diplomacy across</text><text start="329.919" dur="6.161">Southeast Asia for hundreds of years.</text><text start="333.919" dur="4">I&amp;#39;m here today because America is deeply</text><text start="336.08" dur="3.92">committed to the success, sovereignty,</text><text start="337.919" dur="5.201">and prosperity of our many friends and</text><text start="340" dur="6.32">partners, many of whom are at this table</text><text start="343.12" dur="5.359">right now. But partners in this region,</text><text start="346.32" dur="3.599">and we always will be. We&amp;#39;re with you</text><text start="348.479" dur="4.081">always.</text><text start="349.919" dur="5.84">As you know, at last year&amp;#39;s ASEAN</text><text start="352.56" dur="5.28">meeting in Malaysia,</text><text start="355.759" dur="4.081">Prime Minister Anoir and I brokered a</text><text start="357.84" dur="5.199">historic peace agreement between</text><text start="359.84" dur="4.72">Cambodia and Thailand known as the Koala</text><text start="363.039" dur="4.561">Lumper</text><text start="364.56" dur="5.52">Peace Accord. And we secured a ceasefire</text><text start="367.6" dur="5.52">that saved thousands and thousands of</text><text start="370.08" dur="5.679">lives and maybe much more than that. And</text><text start="373.12" dur="5.359">as a result, countless displaced</text><text start="375.759" dur="6">civilians have been able to return to</text><text start="378.479" dur="6.56">their homes. And I was given a big thank</text><text start="381.759" dur="5.521">you from Cambodia. And I was given a big</text><text start="385.039" dur="4.401">thank you from everybody at this table</text><text start="387.28" dur="4.479">for that. That was a great thing. A</text><text start="389.44" dur="4.16">great thing that we did together. We</text><text start="391.759" dur="4.481">remain committed to upholding that</text><text start="393.6" dur="5.039">ceasefire and ensuring full faithful</text><text start="396.24" dur="4.239">implementation of the accord as was</text><text start="398.639" dur="5.441">agreed to one year ago. And I think it</text><text start="400.479" dur="5.121">will hold. getting along quite well. I</text><text start="404.08" dur="3.679">understand</text><text start="405.6" dur="4.64">over the past two years, we have also</text><text start="407.759" dur="4.241">been working closely with many nations</text><text start="410.24" dur="4.799">here tonight to strengthen and deepen</text><text start="412" dur="6.16">our economic relationships with you. The</text><text start="415.039" dur="5.44">United States is setting records. 22.2</text><text start="418.16" dur="6.24">trillion dollars being invested in the</text><text start="420.479" dur="6.961">United States since I took office uh</text><text start="424.4" dur="6.48">less than two years ago. So uh think of</text><text start="427.44" dur="6.319">that 22.2 trillion. That&amp;#39;s many times</text><text start="430.88" dur="5.039">more than any nation has ever had.</text><text start="433.759" dur="4.88">Southeast Asia is one of the busiest</text><text start="435.919" dur="4.4">commercial crossroads on the planet. One</text><text start="438.639" dur="5.761">quarter of the world shipping flows</text><text start="440.319" dur="6.561">through the straight of Mala. And since</text><text start="444.4" dur="5.28">I returned to office, we&amp;#39;ve made major</text><text start="446.88" dur="5.92">trade deals with Malaysia, Cambodia,</text><text start="449.68" dur="5.12">Indonesia, as well as Japan, South</text><text start="452.8" dur="4.88">Korea, and almost everybody, frankly, at</text><text start="454.8" dur="6.32">the table. Just moments ago, I signed a</text><text start="457.68" dur="6.079">new deal with Prime Minister</text><text start="461.12" dur="4.4">Alan Newton of Thailand. Could you stand</text><text start="463.759" dur="5.121">up, Mr. Prime Minister, because that was</text><text start="465.52" dur="4.959">a wonderful thing. He made a much better</text><text start="468.88" dur="3.439">deal than I did, but these are minor</text><text start="470.479" dur="4.72">details.</text><text start="472.319" dur="4.56">Thank you very much. And we&amp;#39;ve made many</text><text start="475.199" dur="4.241">other vital agreements across the</text><text start="476.879" dur="4.481">region, spanning energy, critical</text><text start="479.44" dur="4">minerals, and technology. And I hope</text><text start="481.36" dur="4.72">you&amp;#39;re going to be uh working very hard</text><text start="483.44" dur="5.199">on critical minerals, rare earth, and</text><text start="486.08" dur="3.76">magnets. If you don&amp;#39;t mind, get magnets.</text><text start="488.639" dur="2.481">Somebody at the table is going to say,</text><text start="489.84" dur="3.28">&amp;quot;I&amp;#39;m going to listen to him, and you&amp;#39;re</text><text start="491.12" dur="3.68">going to make a lot of money. We want</text><text start="493.12" dur="4.16">magnets.&amp;quot;</text><text start="494.8" dur="5.6">Thanks to a historic investment from</text><text start="497.28" dur="5.52">South Korea. We also just approved a</text><text start="500.4" dur="5.44">colossal liqufied natural gas pipeline</text><text start="502.8" dur="5.44">in Alaska to facilitate the export of</text><text start="505.84" dur="5.28">record amounts of abundant affordable</text><text start="508.24" dur="5.84">American energy to partners all across</text><text start="511.12" dur="5.279">the Pacific. As you&amp;#39;ve known uh I&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="514.08" dur="4.48">been very strong on that and now we are</text><text start="516.399" dur="5.2">double the size of you add Russia and</text><text start="518.56" dur="5.12">Saudi Arabia together we are much more</text><text start="521.599" dur="5.68">than that. So we are but number one by a</text><text start="523.68" dur="6.64">lot in terms of energy. This historic</text><text start="527.279" dur="5.12">infrastructure project will be something</text><text start="530.32" dur="4.32">very special. It&amp;#39;ll lower energy costs</text><text start="532.399" dur="3.841">and increase energy security for nations</text><text start="534.64" dur="4.16">throughout the region and throughout the</text><text start="536.24" dur="6.48">world. The United States is also leading</text><text start="538.8" dur="6.32">the world in super intelligence SI and</text><text start="542.72" dur="4.88">we have the world&amp;#39;s most powerful SI</text><text start="545.12" dur="5.12">ecosystem. We&amp;#39;re leading everybody by a</text><text start="547.6" dur="5.12">lot and we hope to keep it that way and</text><text start="550.24" dur="4.48">we will keep it that way. And we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="552.72" dur="4.48">excited to work with every country</text><text start="554.72" dur="5.679">represented here today who want to build</text><text start="557.2" dur="6.079">a future for technology and unleash</text><text start="560.399" dur="4.56">enormous economic growth that it brings</text><text start="563.279" dur="4.56">with it.</text><text start="564.959" dur="5.281">They say that uh as an example that</text><text start="567.839" dur="4.241">super intelligence is going to be bigger</text><text start="570.24" dur="4.08">than the industrial revolution. We&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="572.08" dur="4.16">see. But so far it seems to be looking</text><text start="574.32" dur="4">like that far bigger than the internet</text><text start="576.24" dur="3.68">and bigger than the industrial</text><text start="578.32" dur="4.639">revolution. And so it&amp;#39;s enormous</text><text start="579.92" dur="5.2">economic growth creates jobs, unlocks</text><text start="582.959" dur="5.281">the mysteries of science and medicine</text><text start="585.12" dur="4.64">and protects our people, our security,</text><text start="588.24" dur="3.84">and our values. And we have to be</text><text start="589.76" dur="4.8">careful with it like everything else.</text><text start="592.08" dur="5.199">But it&amp;#39;s amazing. And we&amp;#39;ve seen some</text><text start="594.56" dur="4.56">medical cures and medical</text><text start="597.279" dur="4.321">solutions that have been worked on for</text><text start="599.12" dur="6.399">50 years and it&amp;#39;s done in a matter of</text><text start="601.6" dur="6.64">minutes. It&amp;#39;s pretty amazing.</text><text start="605.519" dur="4.32">From energy to technology to security</text><text start="608.24" dur="4.48">and far beyond, there&amp;#39;s no better</text><text start="609.839" dur="5.761">partner on earth than the United States</text><text start="612.72" dur="4.64">of America. Just over two years ago, our</text><text start="615.6" dur="3.919">country was not doing great. We were a</text><text start="617.36" dur="3.68">dead country, frankly. Now, we&amp;#39;re the</text><text start="619.519" dur="3.201">hottest country anywhere in the world.</text><text start="621.04" dur="3.84">And that was said by most of you</text><text start="622.72" dur="4.88">tonight. Didn&amp;#39;t shake you, sir. You&amp;#39;re</text><text start="624.88" dur="4">doing great. Your country is hot. But I</text><text start="627.6" dur="3.12">will tell you, under the past</text><text start="628.88" dur="3.28">administration, we were a dead country.</text><text start="630.72" dur="4.239">We would have been a dead country if</text><text start="632.16" dur="6.239">they won. Under our leadership, American</text><text start="634.959" dur="6.241">exports are at the all-time highest.</text><text start="638.399" dur="4.56">We&amp;#39;ve never had, you know, uh, it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="641.2" dur="3.68">pretty amazing because people thought we</text><text start="642.959" dur="4.56">weren&amp;#39;t a manufacturing country anymore.</text><text start="644.88" dur="6.399">And yet, we just set a record by a lot</text><text start="647.519" dur="6.32">on the all-time high on exports. That</text><text start="651.279" dur="4.641">means manufacturing. US energy</text><text start="653.839" dur="4.24">production is at an all-time high.</text><text start="655.92" dur="4.8">Personal incomes are at the highest</text><text start="658.079" dur="4.481">level ever recorded. And we have more</text><text start="660.72" dur="3.6">people working in America today than</text><text start="662.56" dur="4.399">ever before. We have a record number of</text><text start="664.32" dur="4.639">people working in America.</text><text start="666.959" dur="5.12">And a lot of that&amp;#39;s because of our great</text><text start="668.959" dur="5.44">economic policy. So thanks to our</text><text start="672.079" dur="4.401">unprecedented investments in the United</text><text start="674.399" dur="4.721">States armed forces, America also has</text><text start="676.48" dur="6.88">the strongest and most capable military</text><text start="679.12" dur="6.56">on the planet by far. And we value the</text><text start="683.36" dur="4.96">robust defense partnerships. So we have</text><text start="685.68" dur="4.88">with you and also the equipment we have.</text><text start="688.32" dur="5.04">We make the greatest equipment. You saw</text><text start="690.56" dur="4.399">that in Venezuela. You see it in Iran.</text><text start="693.36" dur="3.039">You see it everywhere. Everybody&amp;#39;s</text><text start="694.959" dur="3.681">buying it. It&amp;#39;s the best equipment</text><text start="696.399" dur="4.481">anywhere in the world. We&amp;#39;re actually uh</text><text start="698.64" dur="4.319">because you have to wait too long. So</text><text start="700.88" dur="4.16">what we&amp;#39;re doing is uh the defense</text><text start="702.959" dur="5.041">companies are now building more than 22</text><text start="705.04" dur="5.68">plants to make Patriots that systems,</text><text start="708" dur="4.72">tomahawks, and everything else. So it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="710.72" dur="3.84">pretty amazing what&amp;#39;s happening. But we</text><text start="712.72" dur="3.92">have the best equipment anywhere in the</text><text start="714.56" dur="4.48">world. Earlier this year, we announced a</text><text start="716.64" dur="5.439">major defense cooperation partnership</text><text start="719.04" dur="5.359">with Indonesia to expand our joint.</text><text start="722.079" dur="4.161">Would you Where is Indonesia? I saw my</text><text start="724.399" dur="5.201">friend here someplace. Would you please</text><text start="726.24" dur="5.279">stand up? He&amp;#39;s such a shy person.</text><text start="729.6" dur="4.96">He&amp;#39;s doing a great job. Thank you very</text><text start="731.519" dur="5.681">much. Congratulations, too.</text><text start="734.56" dur="4.64">Great leader to expand our joint special</text><text start="737.2" dur="4.639">forces training and work together on</text><text start="739.2" dur="5.6">defense modernization.</text><text start="741.839" dur="4.56">We&amp;#39;ve also significantly increased our</text><text start="744.8" dur="4">defense cooperation with the</text><text start="746.399" dur="4.801">Philippines, which has historically been</text><text start="748.8" dur="4.64">a key US ally. But I don&amp;#39;t think we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="751.2" dur="4.96">ever been closer than we are right now</text><text start="753.44" dur="4.639">because of our personal relationship.</text><text start="756.16" dur="4.4">And we support our partners and our</text><text start="758.079" dur="5.281">allies 100%. And when there&amp;#39;s a problem,</text><text start="760.56" dur="5.36">you&amp;#39;ll call me. You&amp;#39;ll call Marco.</text><text start="763.36" dur="5.2">You&amp;#39;ll call others. And if they don&amp;#39;t</text><text start="765.92" dur="4.479">respond, call me. I&amp;#39;ll take your call.</text><text start="768.56" dur="4">I&amp;#39;ll say, &amp;quot;Marco, you&amp;#39;re fired. You</text><text start="770.399" dur="4.401">didn&amp;#39;t you didn&amp;#39;t respond fast enough.</text><text start="772.56" dur="5.2">How hot is Marco? Right. Is Marco doing</text><text start="774.8" dur="5.44">a great job. He&amp;#39;s been fantastic. And</text><text start="777.76" dur="5.759">Scott and Howard, we have a great team</text><text start="780.24" dur="5.039">of people. Jameson, thank you very much.</text><text start="783.519" dur="4.241">They have been really amazing. And the</text><text start="785.279" dur="4.961">trade has been amazing. We&amp;#39;re setting</text><text start="787.76" dur="4.48">every record. So from right here in the</text><text start="790.24" dur="4.719">Philippines to nations across Southeast</text><text start="792.24" dur="4.399">Asia and throughout the Indo-Pacific,</text><text start="794.959" dur="3.921">this is one of the world&amp;#39;s most vibrant</text><text start="796.639" dur="4.561">and productive regions filled with the</text><text start="798.88" dur="3.92">tremendous potential and great friends</text><text start="801.2" dur="4.56">of the United States. You&amp;#39;re great</text><text start="802.8" dur="5.52">friends. I mean, it&amp;#39;s it&amp;#39;s really so</text><text start="805.76" dur="5.04">much better when you know people. I know</text><text start="808.32" dur="4.4">almost all the people at the table and</text><text start="810.8" dur="4.24">it just works so much easier, so much</text><text start="812.72" dur="5.119">better. You know, the good ones, the bad</text><text start="815.04" dur="4.479">ones, the bad ones, too, by the way. but</text><text start="817.839" dur="3.201">you know the the people that you want to</text><text start="819.519" dur="3.681">do business with and it&amp;#39;s so much easier</text><text start="821.04" dur="3.76">and it goes so fast. That&amp;#39;s why we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="823.2" dur="3.6">able to do what we&amp;#39;re doing right now</text><text start="824.8" dur="4.479">and why your area is doing so well. I</text><text start="826.8" dur="4.64">look forward to speaking with many of</text><text start="829.279" dur="4.081">you tonight as we strengthen those bonds</text><text start="831.44" dur="3.76">even further and work to build an</text><text start="833.36" dur="5.76">incredible future for our people and for</text><text start="835.2" dur="5.759">your people, the entire world actually.</text><text start="839.12" dur="4.32">And President Marcos, I want to thank</text><text start="840.959" dur="5.041">you very much. Your family is amazing.</text><text start="843.44" dur="4.959">You&amp;#39;re amazing. And I just met your son</text><text start="846" dur="4.639">who&amp;#39;s a beautiful young man. He&amp;#39;s got a</text><text start="848.399" dur="4.8">great future and it&amp;#39;s an honor to meet</text><text start="850.639" dur="3.921">you, especially to meet you. Okay?</text><text start="853.199" dur="3.041">You&amp;#39;ve done a good job. Your parents</text><text start="854.56" dur="3.04">have done a very good job. So, it&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="856.24" dur="4.48">great honor and thank you very much</text><text start="857.6" dur="5.044">everybody. It&amp;#39;s a real uh special group.</text><text start="860.72" dur="3.944">Thank you.</text><text start="862.644" dur="2.02">[applause]</text></transcript>